    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Do you love riding the Ferris wheel? Have you "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "wondered",
            "ref": "v-wonder"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " why it is called that? The answer is in the name."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "About 130 years ago, the "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Eiffel Tower",
            "zh": "埃菲尔铁塔"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " was "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "built",
            "ref": "v-build"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". It was built for the 1889 "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "World’s Fair",
            "zh": "世博会"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " in Paris. People called it a wonder. Later, Chicago was going to hold the 1893 World’s Fair. The team wanted something better than the tower."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "i1",
        "type": "imageRef",
        "image": "img1"
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "George W. G. Ferris Jr. was an engineer. He built a "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "giant",
            "ref": "v-giant"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "rotating",
            "zh": "转动的"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " wheel. It stood 80 metres tall. It had 36 "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "passenger",
            "ref": "v-passenger"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " cars. Each car could hold about 60 riders. It was the world’s first “Ferris wheel”."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "In just 19 weeks, over one million people rode it. They had a "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "bird’s eye view",
            "zh": "鸟瞰"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " of their city. Today, we’re still calling such rides “Ferris wheels”."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "h1",
        "type": "heading",
        "level": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Famous Ferris Wheels"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The Tianjin Eye, China, the only Ferris wheel built over a bridge."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The London Eye, the UK, (maybe) the most famous Ferris wheel."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p7",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "High Roller, the US, the tallest Ferris wheel."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
